<%# What SpecGuard can read of this run, in the old panel's own words. locals: f (run figures) %>
<% readings = f.readings %>
<% measured_tests = f.measured %>
    <% if measured_tests %>
      <%# The share itself — "N% — X of Y tests carry an @intent." — is stated ONCE, as the verdict card's
          meter (its visible figure and its accessible name). It is deliberately not repeated at the head
          of this note: the same figure twice on one screen is the defect "no figure twice" refuses. %>
      <p class="text-xs text-app-muted" id="intent-reading-basis">
        <% if !readings.recorded? %>
          This run reported suite totals without the per-example rows SpecGuard reads test
          descriptions from, so there is nothing here to say how much of the rest it can
          make out — not that it can make out none of it.
        <% elsif readings.derived.zero? && readings.unreadable? %>
          Of the <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.recorded) %>
          <%= "example".pluralize(readings.recorded) %> this run recorded, SpecGuard cannot
          read <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.unreadable) %> — every one of them that
          carries no @intent. Their descriptions do not give it an entity, an action and a
          behavior, so none of them yielded a reading either.
        <% elsif readings.unreadable? %>
          Of the <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.recorded) %>
          <%= "example".pluralize(readings.recorded) %> this run recorded, SpecGuard reads
          <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.read) %> — the annotated ones and
          <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.derived) %> more from the test's own description
          — and cannot read the remaining <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.unreadable) %>.
          A description is a weaker reading than an @intent: it carries no preconditions, and
          its layer is inferred from the directory rather than declared.
        <% elsif readings.derived.positive? %>
          SpecGuard reads every one of the
          <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.recorded) %>
          <%= "example".pluralize(readings.recorded) %> this run recorded — the annotated ones,
          and the rest from the test's own description, which is a weaker reading than an
          @intent: it carries no preconditions, and its layer is inferred from the directory
          rather than declared.
        <% else %>
          Every one of the <%= number_with_delimiter(readings.recorded) %>
          <%= "example".pluralize(readings.recorded) %> this run recorded carries an @intent
          its author wrote — nothing here is inferred from a test's description.
        <% end %>
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="text-xs text-app-muted">
        The latest run reported no tests at all, so there is no share to take and no coverage
        figure to show — not a coverage figure of zero. That is a fact about this run, not
        about the suite.
      </p>
    <% end %>
